---
// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
import { SITE } from "../data/site";
---

<section id="install" class="install-section" data-section="install" aria-labelledby="install-heading">
  <div class="reading-container centered-section">
    <p class="eyebrow">Quick start</p>
    <h2 id="install-heading">Run Comis on your own infrastructure.</h2>
    <p class="lead">The installer sets up the Comis CLI on macOS or Linux, installs supported prerequisites where it can, and can register the daemon as a service.</p>

    <div class="command-panel">
      <div class="command-line" role="region" tabindex="0" aria-label="Install command">
        <span class="prompt" aria-hidden="true">$</span>
        <code id="install-command" data-install-command>{SITE.installCommand}</code>
      </div>
      <button class="copy-button" type="button" data-copy-button hidden>
        <span data-copy-label>Copy command</span>
      </button>
      <p class="visually-hidden" aria-live="polite" data-copy-status></p>
    </div>

    <p>
      Complete <code>comis init</code>, start the daemon if prompted, then open <code>http://127.0.0.1:4766</code>; the setup wizard can also connect a messaging channel. Linux with Bubblewrap is the recommended deployment target for isolated tool execution.
    </p>
    <a class="text-link standalone-link" href={SITE.installationDocs}>View all installation options</a>
  </div>
</section>

<script is:inline type="module" src="/copy-command.js"></script>
